1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,738
An A.I.

2
00:00:01,738 --> 00:00:06,338
voice agent can call your contacts, ask its questions, leave a message, and

3
00:00:06,338 --> 00:00:08,553
hand a warm customer to a person.

4
00:00:08,553 --> 00:00:12,414
This video shows how to set it up, what the agent does before,

5
00:00:12,414 --> 00:00:15,538
during and after a call, and where you review it.

6
00:00:15,538 --> 00:00:19,740
Calls never connect on this demo site, so the live parts use slides.

7
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,115
An A.I.

8
00:00:25,115 --> 00:00:29,288
call is not a dialer mode, and it does not use a dialer profile.

9
00:00:29,288 --> 00:00:31,314
It is an automated activity:

10
00:00:31,314 --> 00:00:33,639
a contact, a subject, and an A.I.

11
00:00:33,639 --> 00:00:34,474
profile.

12
00:00:34,474 --> 00:00:39,600
The agent calls the contact, talks, and records the outcome like a person would.

13
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:42,383
It works with Telnyx only.

14
00:00:42,383 --> 00:00:45,878
The Asterisk provider cannot place or answer A.I.

15
00:00:45,878 --> 00:00:46,640
calls.

16
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:48,634
Timing matters.

17
00:00:48,634 --> 00:00:53,845
A background task starts due automated activities every five minutes, so the first

18
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:56,154
call can wait up to five minutes.

19
00:00:56,154 --> 00:01:00,358
A workflow task that places the call starts it at once, and skips

20
00:01:00,358 --> 00:01:02,490
the checks you will see later.

21
00:01:06,682 --> 00:01:11,084
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, and choose a starting point.

22
00:01:11,084 --> 00:01:13,344
The Phone calls group has three:

23
00:01:13,344 --> 00:01:19,054
Answer calls at the front desk, Confirm appointments by phone, and Qualify leads by phone.

24
00:01:19,054 --> 00:01:21,671
They need the Automated Voice feature.

25
00:01:21,671 --> 00:01:26,192
Start Qualify leads by phone, give it a title, and create the profile.

26
00:01:26,649 --> 00:01:32,451
The template turns on Start the conversation automatically, and writes an Opening message.

27
00:01:32,451 --> 00:01:34,989
A load refuses a profile without it.

28
00:01:34,989 --> 00:01:38,797
Edit the message in plain words, with your business name.

29
00:01:38,797 --> 00:01:42,967
When a call is not a live audio conversation, this is the first

30
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:44,599
thing the agent says.

31
00:01:48,769 --> 00:01:52,834
An outbound subject has no channel or voice settings of its own.

32
00:01:52,834 --> 00:01:54,867
It has one card for the A.I.:

33
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:56,319
Live agent handoff.

34
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,480
Allow the A.I.

35
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:02,069
to hand off to a live agent, and pick the Handoff queue the call goes to.

36
00:02:02,523 --> 00:02:04,645
Escalate when has three boxes:

37
00:02:04,645 --> 00:02:09,183
the customer asks for a human, the customer is a qualified, ready lead,

38
00:02:09,183 --> 00:02:12,012
and the customer is frustrated or the A.I.

39
00:02:12,012 --> 00:02:13,072
cannot help.

40
00:02:13,072 --> 00:02:16,373
The agent hands off only for the reasons you tick.

41
00:02:16,828 --> 00:02:19,799
The subject flow decides what each outcome does.

42
00:02:19,799 --> 00:02:24,971
Every action has a disposition, and When to choose this disposition is the hint the A.I.

43
00:02:24,971 --> 00:02:27,337
reads to pick one when the call ends.

44
00:02:27,337 --> 00:02:30,198
Write it as a sentence about the conversation.

45
00:02:34,391 --> 00:02:37,779
Open Load Activities, and add an Automatic load.

46
00:02:37,779 --> 00:02:40,289
Pick the Subject and the Campaign.

47
00:02:40,289 --> 00:02:41,167
The A.I.

48
00:02:41,167 --> 00:02:45,811
profile is chosen here, because an outbound subject cannot hold one.

49
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:47,800
Channel is Phone.

50
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,869
Address is the number the customer sees.

51
00:02:50,869 --> 00:02:55,673
Without an address, the Telnyx default outbound caller ID is used.

52
00:02:55,673 --> 00:02:59,876
Schedule at holds the first call until a time you choose.

53
00:03:00,329 --> 00:03:02,579
Save and load the activities.

54
00:03:02,579 --> 00:03:08,749
They wait as automated activities, and the background task starts each one when it is due.

55
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:17,149
Before each call from the background task, the activity is checked.

56
00:03:17,149 --> 00:03:20,774
A number known to be out of service cancels the activity.

57
00:03:20,774 --> 00:03:24,399
So does a contact who opted out of calls on this channel.

58
00:03:25,149 --> 00:03:29,906
With Contact Center Outbound Dialer on, the do-not-call lists are checked too.

59
00:03:29,906 --> 00:03:35,569
A calling window is checked only when your administrator has turned it on for automated calls.

60
00:03:36,319 --> 00:03:40,995
The first reason is written to the activity's notes, and the activity is

61
00:03:40,995 --> 00:03:43,333
cancelled, so it is never dialed.

62
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:48,609
A workflow that places the call starts it directly, and skips all of these checks.

63
00:03:52,809 --> 00:03:55,759
The agent greets with the Opening message.

64
00:03:55,759 --> 00:03:58,831
If recording is announced, it says so first.

65
00:03:58,831 --> 00:04:04,054
With the Contact Center Voice Media feature and a realtime deployment, the call

66
00:04:04,054 --> 00:04:08,539
is a live audio conversation, and the model words its own greeting.

67
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:12,779
Without it, each turn is spoken and transcribed through Telnyx.

68
00:04:13,529 --> 00:04:19,250
If it reaches a voicemail, it waits for the greeting to end, and leaves one message.

69
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:24,589
If nobody has spoken on a call it placed, silence is treated as voicemail too.

70
00:04:25,339 --> 00:04:29,750
If the person goes quiet, the agent asks twice if they are still

71
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:32,522
there, then says goodbye and hangs up.

72
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:38,319
A realtime session that drops is replaced up to two times, with the transcript so far.

73
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:43,403
If the subject allows handoff and a reason you ticked applies, the call

74
00:04:43,403 --> 00:04:45,204
goes to the handoff queue.

75
00:04:45,204 --> 00:04:48,357
The agent who answers sees a summary, labeled A.I.

76
00:04:48,357 --> 00:04:50,946
assistant's summary, written by the A.I.

77
00:04:50,946 --> 00:04:52,409
when it handed over.

78
00:04:56,596 --> 00:05:03,960
In Settings, Contact Center, Recording governance, Tell callers the call is recorded sets the announcement.

79
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:09,891
Have automated voice agents say it first makes the agent say it before anything else.

80
00:05:09,891 --> 00:05:13,996
This tab needs the Contact Center Call Recording feature.

81
00:05:18,219 --> 00:05:20,302
Open a contact's activities.

82
00:05:20,302 --> 00:05:22,936
A finished call shows who handled it.

83
00:05:22,936 --> 00:05:24,957
Dispositioned by reads A.I.

84
00:05:24,957 --> 00:05:31,144
voice agent, with the profile name, and the disposition and the notes hold the agent's summary.

85
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:33,839
The call on this demo site is made up.

86
00:05:34,305 --> 00:05:35,705
Click Review A.I.

87
00:05:35,705 --> 00:05:39,236
conversation to open the full transcript, read only.

88
00:05:39,236 --> 00:05:42,402
The button shows when the activity has an A.I.

89
00:05:42,402 --> 00:05:43,559
conversation.

90
00:05:43,559 --> 00:05:44,959
It needs the A.I.

91
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:47,881
Chat feature, and permission to query A.I.

92
00:05:47,881 --> 00:05:50,195
profiles and to list activities.

93
00:05:51,795 --> 00:05:56,106
An activity that screening cancelled never reaches the agent.

94
00:05:56,106 --> 00:06:01,255
It is cancelled, and the reason, such as an opt-out, is kept in its notes.

95
00:06:05,455 --> 00:06:07,168
Confirm appointments:

96
00:06:07,168 --> 00:06:12,245
call each customer, note cancellations, and transfer changes to your team.

97
00:06:12,995 --> 00:06:14,213
Qualify leads:

98
00:06:14,213 --> 00:06:19,028
call people who asked for information, learn what they need and when, and

99
00:06:19,028 --> 00:06:20,795
transfer the good fits.

100
00:06:21,545 --> 00:06:23,297
Follow up after hours:

101
00:06:23,297 --> 00:06:27,805
use a schedule so calls go out at a time that suits your contacts.

102
00:06:29,805 --> 00:06:30,608
An A.I.

103
00:06:30,608 --> 00:06:32,831
call is an automated activity:

104
00:06:32,831 --> 00:06:39,255
a profile with an opening message, a subject with handoff and dispositions, and an automatic load.

105
00:06:39,255 --> 00:06:42,529
Telnyx places it, and you review it afterwards.

106
00:06:42,529 --> 00:06:44,135
Thanks for watching.

